docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1267:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nModel architecture/workflow diagram labeled “BioBLIP Architecture.” It shows panel-like labels A-D: A indicates multiple input embedding sources (AlphaGenome Ref/Alt embeddings, GenoPT embeddings, ESM Protein embeddings) as blue triangular inputs E1, E2, … En; B shows modality-specific query modules (“DNA Qformer,” “Gene Qformer,” “Protein Qformer”) producing DNA/gene/protein-specific query tokens; C shows a “Master Qformer” receiving query tokens plus an instruction describing genomic variant context and outputting a fixed-length variant prefix; D shows this prefix fed with a text prompt into a “Frozen LLM,” producing a generated variant annotation JSON.\n\nNo quantitative axes or plots are present. The biological/model content shown is a multimodal genomic variant annotation architecture integrating DNA, gene, and protein embeddings for tasks including variant annotation, target gene identification, and regulatory variant prioritization. Main visible finding/claim: BioBLIP uses chained Q-former modules to convert heterogeneous biological embeddings into an LLM-compatible prefix for structured variant annotation.",
