docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2852:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nWorkflow/model architecture diagram for a genomics-language model system. It shows DNA sequences passed through a frozen Evo2-1B model, then a learnable linear projection aligning Evo2 embeddings to Qwen3 dimensions. These projected DNA embeddings are stacked with tokenized text embeddings from a BioReason chat template and Qwen3 tokenizer, using special DNA pad/start/end tokens and a Qwen3 embedding matrix. The combined embeddings feed into a Qwen3-4B model.\n\nVisible labels include “Stacked DNA and Text Embeddings,” “Frozen Evo2-1B,” “Learnable Linear Projection,” “Qwen3 Tokenizer,” “Qwen3 Embedding Matrix,” “BioReason Chat Template,” “Question,” and “Response (with reasoning).” The example biomedical prompt concerns chromosome 12, pathway definition involving LRRK2, CYCS, APAF1, CASP9, and CASP3, and asks about the biological effect of an LRRK2 allele. The response panel gives chain-of-thought-style tags and concludes “Parkinson’s disease.”\n\nMain visible point: the figure illustrates a multimodal architecture combining DNA sequence embeddings with biomedical text prompts to generate disease-related reasoning responses.",
