docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:3256:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nFigure type: workflow/model architecture diagram for a biomedical machine learning method integrating scRNA-seq data and text prompts/labels.\n\nVisible panels/labels: Inputs on the left include “scRNA-seq Data” with a heatmap-like expression matrix labeled row = cell, column = gene, color = expression value, plus “Text (Prompt)” and “Text (Label)” examples. The center shows BioEncoder, LLM Tokenizer, LLM Embedding Layer, CLS/X-pooling, projection layers, and a 2-layer MLP. The right side shows a LoRA module and “LLM Forward Pass,” with training paths labeled S1 and S2. Colored annotations indicate BIO token injection, CT training, and AR auto-regressive training.\n\nQuantity/process shown: It depicts how cell embeddings from scRNA-seq are projected into the LLM token space and injected as soft tokens alongside prompt embeddings, then used to predict label tokens such as a cell type.\n\nMain visible finding/message: The diagram presents a model pipeline for cell-type prediction or annotation using scRNA-seq-derived embeddings combined with LLM prompt/label token embeddings, with optional LoRA fine-tuning and auto-regressive training.",
