docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:3772:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel schematic overview figure for a biomedical AI model/workflow, likely a cell-language foundation model.\n\nFigure type: conceptual workflow/model architecture diagram with labeled panels A-E.\n\nVisible panels and labels:\n- A. Data Sources and Annotations: icons for single-cell data, cell clusters, tissue sections, paper abstracts, and donor metadata. Reported scale includes 800+ datasets, 170M+ single-cell and bulk samples, 100M+ annotations, 21M+ perturbations, and 1B+ tokens.\n- B. Scaling Dimensions: four boxed concepts: Model Capacity, Dataset Size, Multimodality, and Context Diversity.\n- C. Cell Sentence Representation: converts a gene expression matrix with cells and genes into “cell sentences” listing gene tokens.\n- D. Model Training Procedure: three-stage training flow: natural language pre-training with a base LLM, continued training on cell sentences to create C2S-Scale, then instruction fine-tuning for downstream tasks.\n- E. Downstream Tasks: examples include cell type annotation, cell generation, perturbation response prediction, cluster captioning, dataset interpretation, and question answering.\n\nBiological/model quantity shown: scale and modality of single-cell datasets, gene-expression-derived token sequences, and model training/use cases.\n\nMain visible finding/message: the figure presents a unified framework for training a language-model-based system on large-scale single-cell, perturbation, metadata, and text resources, enabling multiple downstream biological interpretation and generation tasks.",
