docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:7026:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure with quantitative plots evaluating an age-prediction or gene-expression model, labeled panels A-F.\n\nPanel A shows histograms of human age groups and mouse age groups, with counts in thousands on the y-axis and age bins on the x-axis. Sample sizes are shown: human N = 18,224 and mouse N = 23,024.\n\nPanel B shows a bar plot of the top-20 tissue counts, with breast, prostate, lung, kidney, and liver among the most frequent tissues.\n\nPanel C shows training and evaluation cross-entropy loss curves over steps, with both curves decreasing and stabilizing around 6.2.\n\nPanel D shows boxplots of Jaccard similarity for upregulated and downregulated genes, comparing P3GPT, GPT4o, and random models. P3GPT appears higher than GPT4o and random, with significance markers.\n\nPanel E compares predicted versus actual human age for Horvathv1 and P3GPT using density plots. P3GPT shows stronger alignment with the diagonal and higher reported correlation, R² = 0.90, than Horvathv1, R² = 0.54.\n\nPanel F is a Pearson correlation heatmap among age-related predictors or clocks, including Horvathv1, Hannum, Lin, PhenoAge, DunedinPACE, DNAmGrimAge, and P3GPT-based. The P3GPT-based measure correlates most strongly with Horvathv1 among the displayed clocks.",
