docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:7222:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel schematic and results figure for the “CellPuzzles” task and “Cell-o1” training strategy. Left panel compares previous LLM-based cell type annotation, requiring no reasoning, with a CellPuzzles batch-level task requiring assignment of unique cell types using expressed genes and donor context, showing example reasoning for cell types such as CD4-positive alpha-beta T cell, CD8-positive alpha-beta T cell, capillary endothelial cell, plasma cell, and respiratory basal cell.\n\nMiddle panel shows the Cell-o1 training strategy with two stages: reasoning distillation, where candidate reasoning is accepted or rejected, and reinforcement learning using a policy model, reference model, reward function, KL term, group computation, and generated answers/rewards.\n\nRight panel contains radial bar-style result plots for cell-level accuracy and batch-level accuracy. A legend compares models including Llama3.1-8B-Instruct, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, Llama3.3-70B-Instruct, GPT-4o-mini, GPT-4o, o3-mini, o1, and Cell-o1. The main visible finding is that Cell-o1 has the highest reported accuracy: 0.68 cell-level accuracy, marked +5.65%, and 0.33 batch-level accuracy, marked +73.05%.",
