docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:7419:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nModel architecture/workflow diagram for generating or modeling single-cell descriptions from gene expression and metadata. It shows a cell with genes `Gene Z`, `Gene E`, ..., `Gene C` passed through a “cell encoder” to produce gene embeddings, then a “modality adapter” projecting dimensions labeled `+512`, `2048`, `3072`. These embeddings are combined with instruction embeddings and prompt embeddings as input to a language model decoder.\n\nLeft side lists cell metadata such as cell type, developmental stage, disease, sex, tissue, and pathway annotations, which form a textual cell description `Cp`. Bottom right shows next-token probability `p`, with the training objective labeled `Lsft = LCrossEntropy(Cp, p)`. Main visible point: the figure illustrates a supervised fine-tuning pipeline aligning single-cell gene/modal embeddings with text generation through a language model decoder.",
