docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:7634:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nFigure type: schematic workflow/model architecture diagram.\n\nVisible labels/panels: The diagram shows a single-cell input sequence labeled “cell 1: Gene Z Gene E ... Gene C,” passed through a “cell encoder” to “gene embeddings,” then through a “modality adapter.” It also shows “Cells Metadata” including cell type, developmental stage, disease, sex, tissue, and pathway terms. These metadata are converted into a natural-language “cell description (Cp).” The lower section shows concatenated “instruction embeddings,” “gene embeddings,” and “prompt embeddings” feeding a “language model decoder,” which outputs “next token probability p.” A loss is shown as cross-entropy, approximately `Lsft = LCrossEntropy(Cp, p)`.\n\nBiological/model quantity shown: Integration of single-cell gene expression embeddings and metadata-derived text prompts into a language-model decoder for supervised fine-tuning or cell-description generation.\n\nMain visible finding/message: The architecture maps single-cell gene information and metadata into embeddings, aligns them through an adapter, and trains a language model to generate a textual cell description using next-token prediction loss.",
