docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:9020:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nWorkflow/model architecture schematic for predicting perturbation response from single-cell data. Left panel shows “Input Single Cell Data” with a colored cell embedding/cluster plot and an RNA-seq gene-by-cell expression heatmap legend for Cell 1, Cell 2, Cell 3, and Cell N. Middle panel, “Preprocessing the Input Modules,” lists meta-labels such as drug doxorubicin 1 µM, CRISPR sgTP53, cell line MCF7, tissue breast, plus cell-sentence tokens including IL7R, LTB, MALAT1, HLA-A, CST7, CCL5, and NKG7, overlaid with a knowledge graph schematic. Right panel, “Generate Perturbation Response,” shows a structured model input with meta-condition token, cell tokens, instruction token, and virtual KG token, followed by model output listing predicted differential-expression changes such as EPCAM up, KRT18 slight-down, MALAT1 down, TOP2A up, and MKI67 down.\n\nMain visible finding: the figure illustrates a multimodal tokenized framework that combines single-cell expression, metadata, and knowledge-graph context to generate gene-level perturbation-response predictions.",
