docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:9329:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel workflow and result figure for a biomedical AI model, CellWhisperer, linking transcriptome embeddings with natural-language text.\n\nPanel a shows a model/training schematic: datasets from GEO metadata, ARCHS4 bulk RNA-seq, and single-cell annotations are converted into sample descriptions and conversations using LLMs; transcriptome and language encoders are trained into a shared 2048-dimensional multimodal embedding space. The application area shows free-text cell labeling and chat-based querying of cell samples.\n\nPanel b shows a UMAP landscape labeled “An annotated landscape of human transcriptomes,” with many colored clusters representing 705,430 GEO transcriptomes in CellWhisperer embedding space.\n\nPanel c shows a UMAP query result for the term “leukemia,” colored by a CellWhisperer score legend from negative blue to positive red. Red-enriched regions indicate transcriptomes matching the leukemia query.\n\nPanel d shows three small histograms of GEO submission dates for selected queried sample groups, including activated myeloid differentiation in HSPCs, K562 erythroleukemia cells in culture, and obese adipose tissue immune/metabolic state.\n\nMain visible finding: the model organizes large-scale human transcriptome data into a shared language-transcriptome embedding space that supports natural-language search, labeling, and biological sample exploration.",
