docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:10426:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure showing a genomic AI model overview and token/task statistics.\n\nPanel a is a biological diagram of sequence-related regulatory and molecular tasks around DNA/RNA/protein contexts. Labels include enhancer, lncRNA, DNA accessibility, promoter, UTR, exon, intron, splice sites, polyadenylation, RNA stability, RNA degradation, protein melting, protein fitness, DNA methylation, histones, and ChatNT as an AI assistant for biological sequences.\n\nPanel b is a horizontal bar plot titled “Number of tokens per task category,” with x-axis “Number of tokens (million)” and legend for English tokens versus DNA tokens. Task categories include promoter activity, expression variants, splice sites, lncRNA, enhancer activity, polyadenylation, promoters, protein fitness, protein melting, enhancers, histones, accessibility, RNA degradation, and DNA methylation. The largest visible DNA-token category is polyadenylation at 361.3M, with enhancer activity also large at 98.0M DNA tokens.\n\nPanel c is a model architecture schematic titled “ChatNT architecture.” It shows DNA sequence tokens entering a DNA encoder, then a DNA resampler, then an English language model. An example prompt asks for degradation rate of a human RNA sequence, and the output states the predicted degradation rate is 1.83.\n\nMain visible finding: the figure presents ChatNT as a sequence-aware language model integrating DNA/RNA/protein biological tasks, with large-scale DNA and English token training data and an encoder-resampler-language-model architecture for biological sequence prediction.",
