docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:11482:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel workflow/model architecture figure labeled **A** and **B**. Panel **A** shows a cross-modal cell-text pretraining pipeline: scRNA-seq/cell omics data and cell description text are tokenized, passed through **Cell Encoder** and **Text Encoder**, aligned by **cross-modal similarity**, and trained with intra-modal cellular generative pretraining plus cross-modal cell-text pretraining. It also includes a retrieval-augmented LLM workflow with **Retriever**, **Database**, **LLM**, and **Reliability Screen** for generating cell type definitions.\n\nPanel **B** shows downstream application of a **pretrained cell encoder** from scRNA-seq/gene expression tokens. Outputs are shown as small UMAP-like embeddings and task panels labeled **Clustering**, **Batch-effect Correction**, **Cell Type Annotation**, **Zero-shot Annotation**, **Few-shot Annotation**, and **Cross-modal Retrieval**.\n\nNo conventional numeric axes are visible. The figure primarily depicts a multimodal single-cell foundation model workflow linking gene expression profiles with text descriptions for cell representation learning, annotation, retrieval, and downstream analysis.",
