docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:12735:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure with experimental genomics/biomedical data. Panels are labeled a-j and include heatmaps, boxplots, contact-map-like triangular matrix, sequence-position effect maps, t-SNE embeddings, bar charts, and phylogenetic/tree diagrams.\n\nVisible content:\n- Panel a: Heatmap comparing protein levels across in-frame stop codons and paired codon substitutions, with a color scale.\n- Panel b: Boxplot comparing RNA half-life change for “Watson” versus “Wobble” categories.\n- Panel c: Triangular mRNA folding probability/contact-style matrix over transcript regions, labeled with 5′ UTR, CDS, and 3′ UTR.\n- Panel d: Boxplots of attention ratio across gene regions, including promoter, tag, 5′ UTR, CDS, and 3′ UTR.\n- Panel e: Horizontal boxplots showing change in protein levels for sequence/region perturbations such as CDS deletion, CDS ribosome-related features, and UTR mutations/deletions.\n- Panel f: Heatmaps showing positional nucleotide effects across transcript sequence regions, including 5′ UTR, CDS, and 3′ UTR; one subpanel marks the start codon.\n- Panel g: t-SNE plots colored by medication type and taxonomy group.\n- Panel h: Horizontal bar chart of feature/category frequencies, with one highlighted red bar.\n- Panel i: Heatmap relating therapeutic area and hosted species labels, with a percentage color scale.\n- Panel j: Tree diagrams comparing transcript/protein length or taxonomic relationships.\n\nMain visible finding: the figure summarizes learned or measured sequence-region effects on RNA/protein outcomes, showing that CDS and UTR features, codon changes, and organism/therapeutic categories are associated with measurable differences in protein level, RNA stability, attention allocation, and sequence-derived structure/features.",
