docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:13376:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nWorkflow flowchart for generating biomedical QA datasets from MANE Select Release 1.4. It shows inputs for protein structures from AlphaFold, amino acid sequences, and DNA sequences, followed by gene annotation with GO terms for biological process, molecular function, and cellular component.\n\nThe pipeline includes system prompt engineering, few-shot example creation, generation of 56 QA pairs per gene/GO aspect using GPT-4.1, LLMOps tracing/analytics in Azure Phoenix, and blinded review by two researchers in Azure Phoenix. A decision diamond labeled “Quality accepted” branches to refactoring prompts if rejected or to final QA generation if accepted.\n\nOutputs are three QA categories: Generic, Denial, and Confirmation, each with 3 QA pairs per gene and GO aspect, totaling about 378,000 samples, leading to final high-quality datasets for model training/evaluation. No quantitative axes or plotted experimental measurements are shown.",
