docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:13688:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nFigure type: schematic workflow/prompt-design panel for biomedical relation extraction.\n\nVisible panels/labels: The left side is titled “Gene–Protein–Phenotype/Disease Contexts” and contains three dashed prompt templates: “Protein molecular features,” “Protein pathogenesis features,” and “Gene inheritance features.” The right side is titled “Instances” and shows one example instance with labeled fields: Gene-entity, Pro-entity, Phenotype, Molecular Summary, Pathogenesis Summary, Disease, and Inheritance Summary.\n\nBiological/model quantity shown: The figure defines text-based inputs used to infer positive or negative associations between gene/protein entities and phenotypes or diseases from molecular, pathogenesis, and inheritance summaries.\n\nMain visible finding/content: The example centers on SERPINA1 / alpha-1 protease inhibitor and A1ATD, with summaries linking protease inhibitor deficiency to emphysema, cirrhosis, and inheritance context.",
