docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:14908:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nSchematic workflow/diagram illustrating a biomedical AI interaction about single-cell gene expression. The panel shows chat bubbles asking for the top 100 primary genes in a randomly selected cell sorted by expression, then inferring cell type, then requesting another endothelial cell. Red gene-name lists include examples such as `GM42418`, `IL1RAPL1`, `GPHN`, `CDK8`, `LARS2`, `JARID2`, `ZC3H7A`, `FGFR2`, and others. \n\nThere are no axes, plots, numerical scales, or legend. A stylized red blood/endothelial-like cell illustration is connected by lines to the gene-list outputs. The main point shown is that gene-expression profiles are used to identify a likely cell type, here labeled “Endothelial,” and retrieve another cell with a similar endothelial gene-expression signature.",
