docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:14993:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nWorkflow and result panel for evaluating a language model on transcriptome embeddings. Left: question-answer pairs from a test set (`n=200`) combine a “transcriptome embedding” with a prompt question (“Describe this sample”) and ground-truth answer (“These are bronchial epithelial…”), passed into an LLM layer. The model outputs a prediction scored by perplexity.\n\nMiddle: scatter/strip plot of perplexity values, with x-axis “Perplexity lower is better” ranging roughly from 1.51 to 14.25 and y-axis categories 1–5. Legend distinguishes gray “Mismatched embeddings (n=30)” and purple “Matched embedding.” \n\nRight: horizontal quantile plot labeled “Perplexity quantiles for all 200 test cases,” showing inverted perplexity quantiles from 0 to 1.0. The visible result emphasizes that matched embeddings tend to have better/lower perplexity quantiles than mismatched embeddings.",
