docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:16294:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel biomedical results figure comparing spatial gene-expression prediction methods across datasets. Panels include boxplots of PCC for methods H2O, OmiCLIP, DeepPT, HistoGene, and BLEEP on ccRCC, PRAD, and IDCLymphNode; horizontal bar charts labeled “Best Gene Prediction Count”; a per-gene PCC comparison plot between H2O and the best competing result; a ranked “PCC Gap” gene plot; an enrichment-style bar chart with `-log10(P-value)` terms; and spatial expression heatmaps.\n\nMeasured quantity is mainly prediction performance using Pearson correlation coefficient (PCC) and normalized gene expression across tissue spots. The visible finding is that H2O generally shows higher PCC distributions and the largest number of best-predicted genes across datasets, with spatial maps appearing closer to ground truth than competing methods for several marker genes.",
