docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:19276:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure showing an interactive single-cell transcriptomics exploration workflow for the Tabula Sapiens dataset using CellWhisperer.\n\nFigure type: workflow/interface screenshot plus UMAP/scatter plots and chat-based annotation panels.\n\nPanels:\n- **a**: Screenshot-style interface labeled “CellWhisperer exploration of the Tabula Sapiens dataset,” showing a UMAP-like embedding, a CellWhisperer score histogram, score-based and visual cell selection, and a chat box.\n- **b**: Large UMAP/scatter plot titled “Cell annotation with free-text query ‘structural cells with immune functions’.” Points are colored by CellWhisperer score with a blue-to-red legend ranging roughly from -8 to 8. Several regions are annotated with inferred cell/tissue descriptions such as macrophages, endothelium, stromal cells, epithelial cells, pericytes, and fibroblasts from decidua tissue.\n- **c**: Chat protocol panel where the user asks about selected cells and immune functions; CellWhisperer responses describe fibroblasts from decidua tissue and mention genes/pathways including COL1A1, COL3A1, COL1A2, MMP1, MMP2, HSPA1A/HSPB1/HSP90AA1, IFITM3, ISG15, JUN, FOS, CCL2, CXCL8, IL6, and extracellular matrix remodeling.\n- **d**: UMAP/scatter plot titled “Mean expression of the genes mentioned by CellWhisperer,” with a green-to-blue/purple expression legend labeled expression log, highlighting the selected cell cluster.\n\nMeasured/shown quantity: CellWhisperer text-query scores and mean expression of genes mentioned in the chat response across single-cell UMAP embeddings.\n\nMain visible finding: a free-text query for “structural cells with immune functions” selects a specific fibroblast-like decidua-associated cell region, and genes discussed by CellWhisperer show elevated mean expression in the selected cell cluster.",
