docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:22891:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific schematic showing a genomic foundation model workflow and biological interpretation.\n\nPanel A depicts the OmniNA model pipeline: pre-training on the NCBI nucleotide database using masked sequence annotation, data processing with prefix-style prompts, and large-scale transformer pre-training. It then shows fine-tuning on genomic tasks such as promoter prediction, mutation pathogenicity classification, and RNA off-target prediction. Labels include “Stage 1: Pre-training on NCBI nucleotide database,” “Stage 2: Fine-tuning for genomic tasks,” “The pre-trained OmniNA,” and “Downstream tasks.”\n\nPanel B is a biological/genomic diagram illustrating chromatin and DNA-level functional genomics. It shows nucleosomes, histone occupation, transcription factor binding, chromosome accessibility, enhancer, promoter, splice site, poly(A) signal, translation initiation site, DNA methylation, and species differentiation across bacteria, archaea, and eukaryotes.\n\nMain visible finding/message: the figure presents a model architecture/workflow for learning from large-scale nucleotide sequences and applying the pretrained model to diverse genomic prediction and functional element characterization tasks.",
