docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:23815:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nWorkflow/comparison schematic with two horizontal panels. The top panel shows a conventional human expert task: input cell clusters with representative marker genes, an expert assigns cell type labels, and output labels include Pulmonary Alveolar Type 2 cells, CD8+ Cytotoxic T Cells, Lung Pericyte, Alveolar Macrophages, and Plasma Cells. The bottom panel shows a “CellPuzzles Task”: given a batch of N cells with contextual metadata and candidate cell types, a model reasons jointly from top expressed genes and cluster/cell relations to determine optimal label assignment, producing labels such as CD4-positive alpha-beta T Cell, CD8-positive alpha-beta T Cell, Smooth Muscle Cell, Lung Macrophage, Non-classical Monocyte, Capillary Endothelial Cell, Plasma Cell, and Respiratory Basal Cell. No axes or quantitative plots are present; the main point is illustrating cell type annotation as a reasoning/assignment workflow.",
