docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:23926:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel model architecture and task schematic for DNA document understanding. Panels are labeled `(a) DNA document generation and visual encoding`, `(b) OCR-style prompt pretraining tasks`, and `(c) Trainable projection, fusion, and decoding`.\n\nPanel `(a)` shows a 1D DNA sequence converted into a multi-page “DNA document” with spatial annotations, then patchified into `p x n x 16 x 16` patches and passed through a frozen visual encoder labeled SAM-Conv, CLIP, producing visual tokens. Panel `(b)` lists pretraining tasks T1-T6: Reading, Grounding, ROI, Completion, Retrieval, and Recognition, with prompts such as “Read the sequence,” “Locate each line in the sequence,” and “Classify document.” Panel `(c)` shows trainable components: projector, multi-page fusion, and document decoder, with prompt/response task instruction flow and loss `L_pt`.\n\nNo experimental plot or numeric biological result is shown; the figure mainly presents a workflow/model architecture for genomic reasoning primitives using visual document encoding of DNA sequences.",
