docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:25181:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nTwo-panel workflow/model figure. Panel A shows a text-prompt style biomedical query with tagged fields such as `<drug> UNKNOWN`, species `m. musculus`, tissue `muscle`, datatype `expression`, up-regulated genes `ORM2 DEFB4B`, down-regulated genes `MUC5AC TBC1D3E MSMB`, and instruction `diff2cpd`; the output lists candidate drugs `metformin`, `semaglutide`, and `acarbose`.\n\nPanel B diagrams a Precious3GPT workflow. The left box shows an input comparison between control age group `20-30 years` and case age group `70-80 years` using an `age2diff` instruction, producing up- and down-regulated gene lists. These gene lists are then passed into another Precious3GPT prompt with a `diff2compound` instruction to output a list of potential geroprotectors.\n\nMain visible finding: the figure illustrates a model pipeline that converts age-associated gene expression differences into candidate anti-aging/geroprotective compounds.",
