docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:26989:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nWorkflow/model overview figure. It has four labeled vertical panels: **Backbones**, **Training Stages**, **Biological Modalities**, and **Evaluation**.\n\nIt shows general-purpose LLM backbones (**Qwen3-1.7B**, **Qwen3-4B**, **Gemma4**) and biological foundation models for **DNA: Evo 2**, **RNA: TranscriptFormer**, and **Proteins: ESM3**. The training pipeline includes **continued pre-training (CPT)**, **supervised fine-tuning (SFT)**, and **reinforcement learning (RL)**. The biological task modalities are **DNA pathway prediction**, **RNA drug target identification**, and **protein function prediction**, illustrated with sequence tokens and simple biological diagrams. The evaluation panel distinguishes **in-domain (ID)** and **out-of-domain (OOD)** settings and lists findings that SFT improves in-domain reasoning, RL enhances out-of-domain performance, and there are trade-offs across stages.",
