docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:27492:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nTwo-panel line plot comparing RNA accuracy across training epochs. Both panels are titled “RNA.”\n\nLeft panel: x-axis “SFT epochs” with ticks 0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32; y-axis “Accuracy” from about 0.2 to 1.0. Multiple model/dataset curves are shown with a legend, including Qwen3-1.7B and Gemma4-E2B variants for ID-Test, OOD-Test, and OV-Test.\n\nRight panel: x-axis “RL epochs” with ticks 0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16; y-axis “Accuracy.” The same model/test split curves are shown.\n\nMain visible finding: accuracy improves rapidly after early SFT epochs, especially for higher-performing OOD/OV curves, while RL curves show a small initial dip around epoch 1 followed by recovery and gradual improvement. Orange Gemma-related curves appear highest overall, near ~0.9 accuracy by later epochs, while blue Qwen ID/OOD curves remain lower.",
