docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:27713:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel experimental result figure comparing age prediction methods. Panel A shows three scatter plots of predicted age versus true age in years for Horvath Clock, Qwen3-14B SFT, and Qwen3-14B RFT, each with a dashed diagonal reference line and reported metrics. Horvath: MAE 4.61, R² 0.895, p 0.946. SFT: MAE 5.91, R² 0.876, p 0.950. RFT: MAE 4.34, R² 0.914, p 0.950. Panel B is a bar chart of MAE in years comparing RFT, Horvath, and SFT, with RFT lowest at 4.34, Horvath 4.61, and SFT highest at 5.91; a significance bracket marks RFT versus Horvath. The main visible finding is that Qwen3-14B RFT gives the best age prediction performance among the shown methods.",
