docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:27807:        "caption": "Figure 1: Landscape of TeamPath (a) Steps of dataset curation. We extract image-text pairs from a processed TCGA dataset (PathGen-1.6M). (b) Word cloud visualization of ROI captions (upper) and questions (bottom). (c) The core visual language model architecture of TeamPath. (d) TeamPath as a system with an LLM-enhanced router (with over 80% accuracy in choosing the correct approach) and the corresponding capacities in various downstream applications. The logo fire means that we need to adjust the parameters of models, and the logo snowflake means that we do not change the parameters. (e) Overall ranking list of different methods across tasks and metrics. A lower rank (larger bubble) means a better method.",
docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:27808:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure showing a pathology vision-language model/data workflow and benchmark results.\n\nFigure type: composite workflow/model architecture plus bubble-plot performance comparison.\n\nVisible panels and labels:\n- Panel a: dataset curation pipeline from whole-slide image to regions of interest, data retrieval, agent summaries, instruct QA pairs, and reasoning QA pairs. Mentions PathGen-1.6M, PathInstruct-Reason, HEST-1K, and STImage1K4M with dataset statistics.\n- Panel c: VLM training architecture with Expert Vis Encoder, Expert Lang Encoder, Expert Lang Decoder, and prompt text.\n- Panel d: TeamPath router-based multi-task system with task-specific instruction, SFT/TTS experts, and outputs for spatial transcriptomic generation, reasoning-driven VQA, reasoning-driven summary, and AI-physician collaboration.\n- Panel e: bubble chart comparing models across pathology VQA splits, pathology summary metrics, and generation metrics.\n\nAxes/legend:\n- Panel e y-axis lists models including TeamPath-7B, PathGen-LLaVA-13B, Patho-R1-7B, Qwen2.5VL-7B, MedGemma-4B, InternVL3-8B, Qwen2.5VL-3B, and MedVLThinker-7B.\n- x-axis metrics include PubMed, SocialPath, Atlas, EduContent, PathCLS, BLEU, ROUGE-1/2/L, BERT, MEDCON, SPCC, GPCC, MSE, and AvgRank.\n- Bubble-size legend indicates rank from 1 to 8.\n\nMain visible finding: TeamPath-7B appears to have the largest/best-ranked bubbles across most VQA, summary, and generation metrics, suggesting strongest overall benchmark performance among the compared models.",
