docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:27900:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel schematic figure showing an RVQ-Alpha model workflow and downstream single-cell analysis tasks.\n\nFigure type: conceptual workflow/model architecture plus task overview diagram.\n\nPanels and labels:\n- Panel a: “Data Encoding Pipeline” converts “scRNA-seq Data” through “RVQ Encoder” into “Discrete Tokens” and “Multi-Task Instruction.” These feed an “RVQ-Alpha Model” trained with “Pretrain & SFT & RL.” The right side shows an “MLLM Architecture” using “Diverse Single Cell Data” with “LLM” and “RVQ” components producing capabilities labeled “Understanding,” “Generation,” and “Reasoning.”\n- Panels b-d: “Downstream tasks” grouped into “Single Cell Task,” “Cell Population Task,” and “Cell Perturbation Task.”\n- Panel b includes cell type identification, top-K gene identification, gene expression generation, and batch effect correction.\n- Panel c includes homogeneous cell type identification, heterogeneous cell type identification, and homogeneous phenotype identification.\n- Panel d includes gene expression change prediction and differentially expressed genes prediction.\n\nVisible biological/model quantities: scRNA-seq-derived cell/gene information, discrete RVQ tokens, cell types, gene expression, perturbation response, batch effects, and differential gene expression.\n\nMain visible finding/message: the figure presents RVQ-Alpha as a multimodal large language model architecture that tokenizes single-cell RNA-seq data and supports multiple downstream single-cell, cell population, and perturbation prediction tasks.",
