docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:28339:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nFigure type: schematic model architecture/workflow diagram for a diffusion-style generative model.\n\nVisible labels/panels: top trajectory shows noisy-to-clean states labeled `x_T`, `x_t`, `x_{t-1}`, `x_0`. Main boxed architecture includes embedder `ϕ`, conditioner `ψ`, encoder `E`, decoder `D`, cross-attention blocks labeled `Q K V`, and variables `x_t`, `x_θ`, `x_{t-1}`, `ε`. Inputs shown include “cell types,” “text,” and “perturbation.”\n\nQuantity/process shown: conditional denoising/generation where biological/text/perturbation conditions are embedded and used via cross-attention in an encoder-decoder network to predict noise or a denoised state.\n\nMain visible finding: not an experimental result; it illustrates how cell-type, text, and perturbation conditioning are integrated into a diffusion model architecture.",
