docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:28713:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel schematic/data overview figure from a biomedical paper. Panel `a` summarizes datasets used for an `H2O` foundation model workflow.\n\nFigure type: dataset/workflow overview with a bar plot, anatomical silhouette, and downstream task dataset icons.\n\nVisible labels and panels:\n- Left: `H2O image FM data` with cylinder icons for `TCGA`, `GTEx`, and `In-house`, showing sample and patch counts.\n- Center: `H2O ST FM and biomodal alignment data`, including a horizontal stacked bar chart by tissue/organ categories and a dataset label `HEST1K`; legend lists cancer/project abbreviations.\n- Right: `Downstream analysis data` with task labels `Temporal`, `3D-Spatial`, and `Multi-omics`, linked to datasets `HTSA`, `OpenST`, and `HTAPP`.\n\nMeasured/shown quantities: numbers of samples, spots, and image patches across biomedical datasets; sample distribution across tissue/cancer types.\n\nMain visible finding: the model is trained/aligned using large-scale histology/image and spatial transcriptomics-related datasets, then evaluated or applied to temporal, 3D-spatial, and multi-omics downstream analyses.",
