docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30964:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel quantitative plot figure with experiment results. Panel **a** shows grouped point/error-bar plots of **Score** across model sizes **14B, 32B, 70B**, split into **Axis** and **Theme** task categories. X-axis labels include biomedical/scientific concept categories such as dataset-related and semantic/theme categories. Legend compares methods: **Base**, **SFT**, **DFT**, **BFT-sample**, **BFT-token**, and **BFT**.\n\nPanel **b** shows line plots of **Regent-1 Score** versus **Model Size** for benchmarks **MsigDB**, **NeST**, and **GeneOntology**, with separate rows/conditions and the same method legend. A green dashed horizontal reference line labeled **GeneAgent** is shown.\n\nMain visible finding: **BFT variants, especially BFT/BFT-token in red/pink, generally improve scores over Base/SFT/DFT across model sizes and benchmarks, with larger models often scoring higher and approaching or exceeding the GeneAgent reference in some settings.**",
