docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:31060:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel workflow/model architecture figure with panels labeled **a**, **b**, and **c**.\n\nPanel **a** shows **data collection and preprocessing** for **scRNA-seq** and protein/network data: “23 cancer types, 234 cell lines,” “12,350 proteins,” an experimentally validated **STRING-E** network, a t-SNE-like scRNA-seq plot, and construction of **75,010 networks**.\n\nPanel **b** shows **model training**: a **large language model** encodes amino acid sequences and functional descriptions into protein embeddings, then a **variational graph autoencoder** with a **GIN encoder**, latent variable **Z**, and decoder performs graph isomorphism/network link prediction for cell-specific networks.\n\nPanel **c** shows **drug target identification** using a “Shushi Model,” fine-tuning on **AML patient scRNA-seq**, link prediction, target identification, and experimental validation.\n\nMain visible finding/message: the figure presents an end-to-end computational pipeline connecting cancer scRNA-seq, protein language-model embeddings, graph neural network link prediction, and drug target discovery/validation.",
