docs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32029:        "description": "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel experiment result figure, labeled Fig. 2, comparing three image-translation methods: HistoPlexer, Pix2Pix-Turbo, and TissueCraftAI.\n\nPanel a is a boxplot of Pearson Correlation Coefficient with y-axis from 0 to 1. TissueCraftAI shows the highest correlation, labeled around 0.915, compared with HistoPlexer around 0.825 and Pix2Pix-Turbo around 0.843. Significance brackets show p-values including p=0.024 and p=0.0076.\n\nPanel b is a bar plot of FID Score. Lower is better visually implied by the comparison: TissueCraftAI has the lowest FID score, 138.4, compared with Pix2Pix-Turbo 209.0 and HistoPlexer 262.8. Significance brackets show p=0.00039 and p=0.00015.\n\nPanel c shows qualitative microscopy/image synthesis examples in a grid. Columns are Input (DAPI), Ground Truth, HistoPlexer, Pix2Pix-Turbo, and TissueCraftAI. Rows show tissue image patches, with predicted histology-like outputs compared to ground truth. PCC values are annotated on generated images. The visible finding is that TissueCraftAI appears closest to ground truth and generally has higher PCC values than the other methods.",
